From: ShareOS <noreply@github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] file: Cache-Control: no-cache for static files on request

A static file is sent with ETag and Last-Modified only, so a browser
decides by itself how long it uses its copy without asking - a tenth of
the file's age. For files that are replaced by an update (the pages of
the apps, the app SDK) that is the old program for hours or days.

With UHTTPD_NO_CACHE in the environment every static file (200 and 304)
carries "Cache-Control: no-cache": kept, but asked for every time.

diff --git a/file.c b/file.c
index 6cb8c45..1071e1f 100644
--- a/file.c
+++ b/file.c
@@ -336,6 +336,8 @@ static char *uh_file_header(struct client *cl, int idx)
 	return (char *) blobmsg_data(cl->dispatch.file.hdr[idx]);
 }
 
+static int no_cache = -1;
+
 static void uh_file_response_ok_hdrs(struct client *cl, struct stat *s)
 {
 	char buf[128];
@@ -347,6 +349,13 @@ static void uh_file_response_ok_hdrs(struct client *cl, struct stat *s)
 	}
 	ustream_printf(cl->us, "Date: %s\r\n",
 		       uh_file_unix2date(time(NULL), buf, sizeof(buf)));
+
+	/* UHTTPD_NO_CACHE in the environment: a browser may keep a file but
+	 * asks every time whether it is still current (answered with 304) */
+	if (no_cache < 0)
+		no_cache = getenv("UHTTPD_NO_CACHE") != NULL;
+	if (no_cache)
+		ustream_printf(cl->us, "Cache-Control: no-cache\r\n");
 }
 
 static void uh_file_response_200(struct client *cl, struct stat *s)
